# =============================================================================
# Dockerfile.bridge-ready -- the offline-capable GEPER image
# =============================================================================
# THIS FILE CANNOT PRODUCE `bridge-ready` ON ITS OWN, AND THAT IS A FINDING
# RATHER THAN AN OMISSION. Read this header before assuming a step is missing.
#
# `bridge-ready` is the base image plus the 4.6 GB offline model-cache seed.
# THE SEED CANNOT ENTER AN IMAGE THROUGH THE BUILD CONTEXT. Its HuggingFace
# layout contains five relative symlinks
# (models--facebook--esm2_t33_650M_UR50D/snapshots/<sha>/* -> ../../blobs/<sha>)
# and BuildKit refuses to load a context containing them:
#
#     ERROR: invalid file request model_cache_seed/models--facebook--
#     esm2_t33_650M_UR50D/snapshots/08e4846e.../config.json
#
# Measured three times by three agents on three different Dockerfiles, which
# is why `.dockerignore` now excludes the seed BY DESIGN -- without that line
# the repository does not build at all from a checkout that has the seed on
# disk. `docker cp` fails too, and worse: it prints
# `unknown file mode ?rw-rw-rw-`, continues, exits zero, and leaves the blobs
# whole and the pointers gone.
#
# The only mechanism that carries them is a RUNTIME BIND MOUNT, and that is
# not a Dockerfile instruction. So the image is produced by this file PLUS one
# named, scripted, committed step: `scripts/build_bridge_ready.sh`.
#
# THE STEP IS EXPLICIT ON PURPOSE. The existing `geper:bridge-ready` was
# hand-assembled, and `docker history` cannot say how its files arrived --
# it records the command a layer ran, never the `docker run` flags behind it.
# A Dockerfile that looked complete while quietly depending on an unwritten
# hand step is the exact defect this replaces.
#
# BUILD (do not invoke this file directly -- the script drives both halves):
#     scripts/build_bridge_ready.sh --base geper:latest --tag geper:bridge-ready
#
# =============================================================================

# The base built by the tracked `Dockerfile` (docker-compose tags it
# `geper:latest`). Declared as an ARG rather than hard-coded so the seed step
# can be re-run against a rebuilt base without editing this file.
ARG BASE_IMAGE=geper:latest
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}

# --- The cache location, which is the whole of what a Dockerfile CAN do here.
#
# `/app/model_cache_seed` is chosen because it is NOT a declared VOLUME, and
# that is load-bearing rather than cosmetic. The base image declares
# /app/geper/geper_output, /app/geper/model_cache and /root/.cache/huggingface
# as volumes, and `docker commit` DOES NOT CAPTURE VOLUME CONTENTS -- a seed
# written to any of them builds cleanly, commits cleanly, and is ABSENT AT RUN
# TIME. The two most obvious places to put a model cache are both traps, and
# the tracked Dockerfile's own `GEPER_CACHE_DIR=/app/geper/model_cache` points
# at one of them.
#
# All three variables point at the same directory, and they are NOT
# interchangeable -- seeing them equal here is exactly what invites the
# mistake:
#   GEPER_CACHE_DIR  GEPER's own cache root; every loader derives its subpath
#                    from it (TORCH_HOME, HYENADNA_CHECKPOINT_DIR, ...).
#   HF_HUB_CACHE     the HuggingFace hub cache ROOT. This is the one that
#                    matters for ESM2 and the one that used to be wrong.
#   HF_HOME          HuggingFace's home directory. Setting only this sends the
#                    library to $HF_HOME/hub -- one level too deep. An earlier
#                    image had HF_HOME=/app/model_cache_seed/hf and therefore
#                    searched a directory that did not exist while the models
#                    sat at the root. Symptom: a full-looking cache and a miss.
ENV GEPER_CACHE_DIR=/app/model_cache_seed \
    HF_HUB_CACHE=/app/model_cache_seed \
    HF_HOME=/app/model_cache_seed

# --- HyenaDNA's vendored source, WITHOUT WHICH THIS IMAGE IS NOT OFFLINE.
#
# MEASURED, NOT ANTICIPATED: with only /app and /app/geper on the path, a
# HyenaDNA load under `--network none` fails with
#   `fatal: unable to access 'https://github.com/HazyResearch/hyena-dna.git/':
#    Could not resolve host: github.com`
# -- the image reaches for GitHub at model-load time. Three of four models
# loaded; this was the fourth.
#
# The mechanism is a bare CWD-relative path in the loader
# (`geper/models/hyenadna.py`: `repo_dir = "./hyena-dna"`). It first asks
# `importlib.util.find_spec("standalone_hyenadna")`, and only if that fails
# does it clone. The vendored source IS in the image, at
# /app/geper/hyena-dna -- but `./hyena-dna` resolves against the working
# directory, which is /app, so the loader cannot see what is already there
# and tries to fetch it.
#
# That was first fixed HERE, by putting the vendored directory on PYTHONPATH
# so `find_spec` succeeded and the clone branch was never entered. THAT ENTRY
# HAS SINCE BEEN REMOVED DELIBERATELY, and this comment exists so that the
# PYTHONPATH below is not read as under-specified and "repaired".
#
# WHY IT IS GONE. The real defect was in the loader, and it is fixed there
# now: `geper/models/hyenadna.py` resolves the vendored checkout from
# `__file__` instead of from the working directory. Once the module finds its
# own source, the ENV entry is LOAD-BEARING FOR NOTHING.
#
# *** DO NOT RESTORE IT. *** It would not be inert. `/app/geper/hyena-dna` on
# PYTHONPATH makes `find_spec("standalone_hyenadna")` succeed no matter where
# the process was launched from -- which means it SILENTLY ABSORBS any future
# regression of the module's path handling. The offline proof would stay green
# while the loader was broken again. Removing this entry is precisely what
# gives that proof the ability to fail.
#
# The removal is tested, not assumed: with this line absent and the module
# fix in place, all four models construct under `--network none` from /var/tmp,
# / and /app/geper. With this line absent and the OLD module, HyenaDNA fails
# with `Could not resolve host: github.com` -- the negative control that makes
# the pass mean something.
ENV PYTHONPATH=/app:/app/geper

# Created here so the directory exists with the right ownership even before
# the seed step runs; an image built from this file alone is a valid,
# network-dependent GEPER image, not a broken one.
RUN mkdir -p /app/model_cache_seed

# The acceptance test travels IN the image, so the image can be verified
# wherever it lands rather than only on a machine that has this repository.
COPY scripts/verify_offline_models.py /app/scripts/verify_offline_models.py

WORKDIR /app

# No ENTRYPOINT and no CMD, deliberately: the base image documents three
# independently valid ways to run this pipeline and hard-coding one would make
# the other two second-class. That decision is the base image's; this file
# does not overturn it.
